 "notes": [
  "IHS MARKIT MERGER closed 28-Feb-2022; GAAP Q1-22 includes IHS Markit from the acquisition date (one month). New segments: Commodity Insights (Platts + IHS Markit resources; code CI), Mobility (MOB), Engineering Solutions (ES). Segment order as published: MI, Ratings, CI, Mobility, Indices, ES. New IS / segment line 'Equity in Income on Unconsolidated Subsidiaries' (income 3; OSTTRA JV).",
  "ADJUSTED FIGURES ARE PRO FORMA (as if merger closed 1-Jan-2021, excluding divested businesses). Because they include IHS Markit pre-acquisition results and use pro forma share counts, they are stored under *_pf keys (adj_op_pf, adj_ni_pf, adj_eps_pf, seg adj_op_pf, adj_corp_pf ...); ngaap.adj_op / adj_ni / adj_eps (actual-scope adjusted) are NOT published for Q1-22 and are omitted. Pro forma bridge lines are stored separately (pf_ihs_pre_acq, pf_ihs_pre_acq_amort, pf_ihs_one_time, pf_divest) and are not ngaap items.",
  "Gain on dispositions printed (1,344) = gain: gain_disp = +1,344 (mainly MI divestitures: CUSIP Global Services, LCD). Equity income printed (3) = income: eq_inc = +3. 'Other income, net' (49) = income: oth_inc = +49.",
  "Loss on extinguishment of debt, net 17 is a separate IS line below operating profit; kept in other_lines (as -17, income sign). EBT 1,867 = 1,892 + 49 - 57 - 17; check_rec 'op+oth-int = ebt' therefore fails by 17 (no schema key for this line; published values kept).",
  "Market Intelligence segment expenses printed (762) (negative) because the gain on disposition is netted in segment expenses; segment expense total 497 vs IS expenses 1,844.",
  "MI gain on disposition: footnote prints '$1.3 billion ($1 billion after-tax)'; pre-tax recorded as -1,344 from the IS 'Gain on dispositions' line (all in MI: MI non-GAAP adjustments 1,324 = 1,344 - 18 - 2, computed); after-tax recorded as printed (-1,000). Implied after-tax from the aggregate line = -473 - 548 (other items) = -1,021 (computed, not used).",
  "Corporate footnote items sum to 492 pre-tax vs 'Non-GAAP Adjustments (g)' printed 490 (rounding).",
  "Indices pro forma adjusted operating profit attributable to the Company: 176 (NCI share 59).",
  "Exhibit 5 ETR table prints 'Adjusted interest expense, net | \u2014 ' for 2022 (garbled; the interest table gives adjusted pro forma interest 91; 1,388 + 45 - 91 = 1,342 ~ adjusted pre-tax 1,343).",
  "corp_nongaap / corp_deal_amort in add-back sign (reduce unallocated expense).",
  "cfpub three months; capex and nci_dist recorded as positive outflows. 'Pro Forma Free cash flow excluding certain items' 701.",
  "rev_type_pf is the PRO FORMA revenue by type (Exhibit 6); no actual-scope revenue-by-type table is published.",
  "Guidance updated vs 1-Mar-2022 guidance: GAAP EPS previously $13.40-$13.60; adjusted PF EPS previously $13.30-$13.50; PF FCF excl. items previously $4.9-$5.0bn; PF revenue previously mid-single-digit growth.",
  "Ratings has no pro forma revenue adjustment rows in Exhibit 5; its adjusted PF revenue (868 / 1,017) is taken from the Exhibit 6 by-type table (404+464, 582+435) \u2014 computed."
 ],
